.TH WGET 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
wget \- download a file from the internet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wget
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-O
.IR file ]
.I url
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wget
downloads what
.I url
names, through the computer's internet card, following redirects, into a
file named as the URL's last part
.RB ( index.html
when it has none). A URL without a scheme is
.BR http:// 's.
It says what it does on standard error.
.PP
The card reaches only the public internet: never the server's own machine
or network (the server's settings may allow more, or less).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
Says nothing.
.TP
.BI \-O " file"
Saves to
.I file
instead
.RB ( \- :
standard output).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when it saved the file; 2 for bad usage; 3 when the file can't be written;
4 for a network failure (refused, an unknown host, timed out); 8 when the
server answered with an error (4xx, 5xx).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wget https://example.com/
wget \-O notes.txt https://example.com/notes
.fi
.SH NOTES
GNU
.BR wget 's
recursion, retries and resuming
.RB ( \-r ,
.BR \-t ,
.BR \-c )
are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
